  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police (Polri) has deferred a scheduled ethics hearing for Irjen Slamet Uliandi, who is facing scrutiny over his alleged involvement in unauthorized wiretapping activities and treasonous conduct directed at President Prabowo Subianto. Police spokespeople confirmed that the Commission for Police Professional Ethics postponed the proceedings because the officer is currently receiving medical treatment at a hospital. Under standing regulations, the subject of an ethics inquiry is generally required to be present in person for the duration of the trial. While these developments regarding Slamet Uliandi are underway, concurrent institutional attention remains focused on the broader ethics investigations involving high-ranking officials within the force, including sessions involving five three-star generals tasked with presiding over related police disciplinary matters.",
